id: pm-y3w0ld
title: "GH-864: history-redact output must never echo literal secrets"
description: "GitHub issue #864 demonstrates that the audited redaction mutation rewrites history safely but returns the original literal matcher under patterns.literals, copying the value into terminal logs, CI output, agent transcripts, and SDK/MCP responses. Make the result contract disclosure-safe across applied, dry-run, no-op, and failure paths while preserving deterministic matcher counts and auditability."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:sdk","area:security",history,privacy,redaction
created_at: "2026-08-02T00:40:15.547Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-02T02:00:53.021Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-02T02:00:52.175Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-02T02:00:52.175Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Raw literal matcher values are absent from TOON, JSON, SDK, MCP, dry-run, no-op, error, telemetry, and profile outputs; regex matcher source receives equally safe treatment because pattern text may itself be sensitive; results retain deterministic matcher-kind counts and replacement/change counts without reversible matcher material; regression tests use canary matchers and assert absence from serialized success, dry-run, no-op, and failure surfaces; public SDK types and operator documentation define the disclosure-safe result contract; full 100/100/100/100 coverage, security scan, contract gates, and isolated temporary-directory acceptance pass"
goal: project management = context management
objective: A secret supplied for audited removal is never repeated by the command that removes it
value: "History redaction must reduce disclosure, never multiply it into output and observability surfaces"
impact: "Changes the public HistoryRedactResult pattern summary to non-reversible metadata and hardens CLI, SDK, MCP, telemetry, and tests against canary disclosure"
outcome: "Applied, preview, no-op, and rejected redaction invocations expose useful counts without returning matcher content"
parent: pm-4a7m
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Disclosure-safe history-redact output across CLI, SDK, MCP, recovery, telemetry, and profiling"
expected_result: "No supplied literal, regex source, or replacement is reflected by any success or failure surface; useful non-reversible counts remain"
actual_result: Canary acceptance and 136 focused tests prove non-disclosure including four review edge cases; 6692 tests and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage plus strict gates pass
