  "2026-08-02T01:25:27.533Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: public HistoryRedactResult now exposes matcher-kind counts and replacement_is_default only; CLI recovery and typo guidance sanitize history-redact argv; telemetry redacts literal/regex/replacement inputs while retaining safe count fields; CLI, SDK, MCP, telemetry, dry-run, no-op, applied, and rejected paths have canary non-disclosure coverage. The public SDK surface records the acknowledged GH-864 security contract change."
  "2026-08-02T01:25:33.533Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: final source head passes 417/417 test files and 6691/6691 tests with exact 100% statements (47379/47379), branches (34105/34105), functions (9641/9641), and lines (45975/45975). pnpm lint passed with zero ESLint warnings and zero duplication clones; static quality passed 100% docstring/export/member coverage and SDK/package/token/context gates; contracts, secrets, docs links, context/retrieval/agent-task token evaluations, SDK surface, typecheck, and focused 63-test matrix passed."
  "2026-08-02T01:28:11.945Z","harness:codex","Changelog evidence: npm registry latest pm-changelog is 2026.8.1; package-owned generation added the Unreleased security entry and changelog:pm:check reproduced it byte-for-byte."
  "2026-08-02T01:29:54.208Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/869 opened from exact implementation commit 0761e4fd8. The PR links this canonical item and closes GitHub issue #864; final exact-head review/check evidence will be appended after CI and bot review."
  "2026-08-02T01:36:46.411Z","harness:codex","Review round 1: CodeRabbit reported four actionable findings at head 178917ac6: plural inline telemetry assignments, inherited recovery payload fields, sensitive equals-form flag typos, and value-less sensitive flags followed by another option. All four were verified against current code and are being fixed; CI otherwise passed every required check."
  "2026-08-02T01:40:20.781Z","harness:codex","Review fixes implemented: plural inline assignment patterns are redacted; existing compact/expanded recovery fields are rebuilt from sanitized argv; sensitive typo source and canonical equals-form values are redacted; and value-less sensitive flags preserve following options. Focused ESLint, typecheck, and 136 tests pass."
  "2026-08-02T02:00:45.358Z","harness:codex","Review-fix verification: final refactored head passes 417/417 files and 6692/6692 tests with exact 100% statements (47395/47395), branches (34132/34132), functions (9645/9645), and lines (45991/45991). Full lint/static/docstring/zero-duplicate, contracts, security, docs links, SDK surface/import cost, CLI transport, token budget, and context calibration gates pass."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T01:25:29.335Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance used an unrelated temporary tracker and exercised dry-run, applied, no-op, and invalid-regex paths. All matcher and replacement canaries were absent from captured stdout/stderr; applied history verified successfully and added the audit marker only when a rewrite occurred."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T01:25:31.961Z","harness:codex","Inputs supplied to a redaction primitive are sensitive by purpose, even when they do not resemble credentials. Disclosure safety must cover success results, failures, recovery bundles, telemetry, profiling, and transport adapters; counts are the useful non-reversible substitute."
